  "note": "enemy_seam_arbiter (R7 Hollow Orchard, Boundary Survey; arbiter/boundary; architectural, scale large, motion seam_ruling). Author design: two tall weathered orchard-wood panels braced like a door and split by a chalk-white seam, a heavy ruling beam across the top with bare orchard branches growing from it, chalk boundary marks and tally strokes, hanging survey tags, all on a low sledge base (support reference: FAM-ARPG-17 Seam Bailiff, same region: braced doorway, chalk seam, low moving base). Tall, cold and wooden so it never reads like the squat iron Kiln Door Ward. Telegraph: the beam lifts, the panels part and the seam shows cold light. Signature (boundary ruling, ice): the beam slams down and frost spreads from the seam over the base. Break (recorded): right panel tipping, beam askew, a branch snapped. Phase 1 First Ruling: record sheets pinned on the panels, a bronze plate on the beam. Phase 2 Final Ruling: panels swung apart, the seam gaping open. Front battler, 60 deg view.",
